Each file is one 128-byte EDID base block.

t14-n140hca-eae.bin, amd-bench-b140han06.8.bin: each laptop's panel, as its
firmware publishes it through EFI_EDID_ACTIVE_PROTOCOL, read by the loader on a
metalcase boot (PR #895's M1 reading; EDID Discovered gave the same bytes).
Both had their ID serial (bytes 0x0C-0x0F) zero already and carry no 0xFF
serial descriptor, so nothing was zeroed and each checksum is the panel's own.
Their first descriptors give 309x173 mm (T14) and 309x174 mm (AMD bench).

qemu-*.bin: the base block QEMU 11.1.1's generator writes, by `qemu-edid -o`
with no option (default), and with `-x 2560 -y 1600 -d 254`,
`-x 3456 -y 2234 -d 254` and `-x 1920 -y 1080 -d 157`.

virtio-gpu-get-edid-1024x768.bin: QEMU 11.1.1's virtio-gpu-pci, xres=1024,
yres=768, answering VIRTIO_GPU_CMD_GET_EDID for scanout 0.
